+# Exact standard-library endpoint controls
+
+The port replaces all SymPy matrix and eigensolver operations with exact pairs of Fractions representing Gaussian rationals. Native Pauli A and oriented cycle S are built separately from Jordan–Wigner gamma matrices and their even-Fock restriction. Flux-projected native traces match the independently constructed CAR traces through the full sector dimension.
+
+Newton trace identities give the characteristic polynomial of iK. The triangle polynomial is x(x²−12); square flux− is x²(x²−16); square flux+ is (x²−8)². Independent closed-form energy moments test the original spectra and spectator multiplicities. This covers the odd-vertex dictionary example, active zero modes, total sector/native dimensions and the factor2 in K without a numerical eigensolver.
+
+Eighty explicit predicates pass under-OO in0.04753s17.266MiB. Counts are newly declared, not a claim that the original54 SymPy checks were byte-preserved. Their spectra and mathematical targets are unchanged, and original sources/proof/review remain archived. The independent reviewer's508 gauge-isometry controls are archived but not ported or rerun; this helper does not claim their separate coverage.
+
+Three actual isolated subprocess mutations fail: K factor2 removed, odd matter domain substituted, and spectator multiplicity halved. The odd/even spectra alone are identical because spectator modes absorb parity; therefore a spectral test would not discriminate the wrong physical domain. The explicit global-Gauss-product check does discriminate it and is recorded honestly. No native phase was removed in the correct computation. No cubic flux optimum, sampling, phase or physical selector is claimed.
